.TH "EVENT.TIMESTAMP" "3JS" "September 1, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Event.timeStamp \- Event: timeStamp property
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]timeStamp\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]Event\f[R] interface returns the time (in milliseconds) at which
the event was created.
.SH VALUE
The value is a \f[CR]DOMHighResTimeStamp\f[R] representing the number of
milliseconds elapsed from the relevant global object\(cqs time origin
until the event was created.
Its precision may be reduced to mitigate timing attacks and
fingerprinting.
.SH EXAMPLE
.SS HTML
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]p\f[R]>
  Focus this iframe and press any key to get the current timestamp for the
  keypress event.
</\f[B]p\f[R]>
<\f[B]p\f[R]>timeStamp: <\f[B]span\f[R] id=\(dqtime\(dq>\-</\f[B]span\f[R]></\f[B]p\f[R]>
.EE
.SS JavaScript
.IP
.EX
\f[B]function\f[R] getTime(event) {
  \f[B]const\f[R] time = document.getElementById(\(dqtime\(dq);
  time.firstChild.nodeValue = event.timeStamp;
}
document.body.addEventListener(\(dqkeypress\(dq, getTime);
.EE
.SS Result
.SH REDUCED TIME PRECISION
To offer protection against timing attacks and fingerprinting, the
precision of \f[CR]event.timeStamp\f[R] may be reduced depending on
browser settings.
.PP
Fractional milliseconds do not necessarily mean that time precision has
not been reduced.
.PP
In Chrome, the rounding interval is 0.1 ms, or 0.005 ms in
cross\-origin\-isolated contexts.
In Safari, it is 1 ms, or 0.02 ms in cross\-origin\-isolated contexts.
.PP
In Firefox, the \f[CR]privacy.reduceTimerPrecision\f[R] preference is
enabled by default and uses a rounding interval of 1 ms, or 0.02 ms in
cross\-origin\-isolated contexts.
If \f[CR]privacy.resistFingerprinting\f[R] is enabled, the rounding
interval is 16.667 ms or the interval configured by
\f[CR]privacy.resistFingerprinting.reduceTimerPrecision.microseconds\f[R],
whichever is larger.
.PP
For example, these are possible values in Firefox:
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// Reduced time precision (1 ms) in a non\-isolated context\f[R]
event.timeStamp;
\f[I]// Might be:\f[R]
\f[I]// 9934\f[R]
\f[I]// 10363\f[R]
\f[I]// 11671\f[R]
\f[I]// \&...\f[R]

\f[I]// Reduced time precision with \(gaprivacy.resistFingerprinting\(ga enabled\f[R]
event.timeStamp;
\f[I]// Might be:\f[R]
\f[I]// 10000.2\f[R]
\f[I]// 10016.867\f[R]
\f[I]// 10033.534\f[R]
\f[I]// \&...\f[R]
.EE
